{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 44, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and a leader of the Crusader state of Tripoli. He was born in 1140 and was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *Early Life* Raymond III succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli at a young age after his father's assassination in 1152. His mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age.\n\nRaymond III was taken captive by Nur ad-Din Zangi in 1164 during the Battle of Harim. He was released in 1173 after being held captive for nearly a decade. During his captivity his mother Hodierna had died and his county was being managed by others. Upon his release he returned to Tripoli and took control of his county. *Reign* Raymond III was a skilled military leader and expanded his territory through various campaigns. He also played a significant role in the politics of the Crusader states and was a key figure in the Kingdom of Jerusalem.\n\nIn 1174 Raymond III supported Miles of Plancy as regent for King Baldwin IV of Jerusalem. However he soon changed his allegiance and supported the candidacy of Raymond of Poitiers' widow Constance's choice for regent. Raymond III was appointed as regent for King Baldwin IV in 1177 and he played a crucial role in the king's early reign. *Regency for Baldwin IV* As regent Raymond III was responsible for making key decisions on behalf of the young king. He worked to maintain the fragile peace between the Crusader states and their Muslim neighbors. He also oversaw the military campaigns against the Zengid forces.\n\nRaymond III's regency ended when King Baldwin IV came of age. He continued to play a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and was a key advisor to the king. He died in 1187 without an heir and his county was inherited by his godson Raymond IV. Raymond III's legacy is complex and his role in the events leading up to the Battle of Hattin is still debated among historians. He is remembered as a skilled military leader and a shrewd politician who played a significant role in the history of the Crusader states.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.011065074242651463}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0003358753747306764}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0013428251259028912}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.1729656308889389}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.05285166576504707}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.9150496125221252}, {"token": " leader", "logprob": -0.2793315052986145}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0024888513144105673}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.700400710105896}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " state", "logprob": -0.1699860394001007}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.010913563892245293}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.08265946060419083}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.006036384031176567}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.00022015532886143774}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.00012385078298393637}, {"token": " born", "logprob": -0.023710520938038826}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.6931589841842651}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.16052407026290894}, {"token": "114", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.0005534547381103039}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.6971679925918579}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -4.660974445869215e-05}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.00010084597306558862}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.00027807659353129566}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "lo